# AY <-> z3 reference-oracle PIN: the one statement of WHICH z3 bytes the differential gate is measured against.
#
# WHAT IT PINS. The upstream GitHub release asset of z3, per platform row: the archive's name, size and sha256 (equal
# to GitHub's own asset digest when the pin was cut), and the sha256 of the archive's bin/z3. scripts/_z3_reference.py
# downloads the row for this host, checks both hashes, and unpacks it read-only into the content-addressed user cache
# ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/ay-z3/<archive sha256>/. No machine-wide install is involved, and nothing is built.
#
#     python3 scripts/_z3_reference.py --provision   # once per host; prints the bin/z3 path
#     python3 scripts/_z3_reference.py --path        # offline; exit 2 when not provisioned
#
# WHY BYTES AND NOT A VERSION. The differential gate (scripts/differential_gate.sh) used to admit any program whose
# --version banner named the right version, and its bypass flag still ended in a passing verdict. A banner is not an
# identity: a source build, a patched build and a drop-in all print it. The gate now admits its oracle by the sha256
# of bin/z3 against this file; any other oracle can still run, but the run ends `GATE: PASS-UNPINNED` with exit 4,
# never `GATE: PASS`.
#
# WHAT THE BYTES ARE. No row's bin/z3 loads libz3 (Mach-O load commands and ELF NEEDED entries name only the C/C++
# runtime and libc), so hashing bin/z3 pins z3's own code; the C++ runtime and libc are the host's. Z3_REFERENCE_ROW
# is the row the dated gate measurements of 2026-09-24/25 ran: they name the oracle by its unpacked path, and
# the development design notes:72 is that path, whose bin/z3 is this file's darwin_arm64 bin sha256.
# The 2026-09-30 chc-family measurement names only a version and recorded no bytes. From this pin on, every gate run
# records its oracle (path, sha256, banner, row) in the run directory's plan.json, and `--observed` output starts
# with the same identity, so a ledger edit cites the bytes that produced it. Other rows are the same release built
# for other platforms; the gate admits them with a NOTE.
#
# FORMAT: strict KEY=VALUE, no spaces, no quoting, no expansion, like ci/veripb.pin and ci/cakepb.pin; `.`-able from
# POSIX sh and read by the hand-written parser in scripts/_z3_reference.py, which refuses an unknown or duplicated
# key, a malformed sha or size, an asset name that does not carry the version, a URL that does not end in the
# version's tag, and a row with a missing or orphan key. Z3_ROWS lists the rows; each row has the four keys
# Z3_ASSET_<row>, Z3_ASSET_SIZE_<row>, Z3_ASSET_SHA256_<row> and Z3_BIN_SHA256_<row>. The release tag is
# "z3-" + Z3_VERSION and is not restated.
#
# TO MOVE THE PIN:
#   1. `agh api repos/Z3Prover/z3/releases/tags/<tag>` gives the asset names, sizes and digests.
#   2. `python3 scripts/_z3_reference.py --measure <asset url>` per row gives the bin/z3 sha256 and its dynamic
#      dependencies. A row whose bin/z3 loads libz3 must also pin that library, or be dropped.
#   3. Re-measure the floors and the ledger with the new oracle (full budget, `--observed`; re-solve every timeout
#      at -T:15, per scripts/differential/README.md). The `--observed` header carries the oracle line.
#   4. Commit this file and scripts/differential/KNOWN_WRONG.tsv together, and rewrite this prose to match. A run
#      made under the old pin rejudges as PASS-UNPINNED under the new one.

# Upgraded 2026-11-06. All four archives match upstream release sizes/digests;
# executable hashes were measured from the exact release archive members.
# Previous 5.1.0 measurements remain historical; this pin makes no fresh sweep claim.
Z3_VERSION=5.3.3
Z3_RELEASE_URL=https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3/releases/download/z3-5.3.3
Z3_REFERENCE_ROW=darwin_arm64
Z3_ROWS=darwin_arm64,darwin_x86_64,linux_x86_64,linux_aarch64

Z3_ASSET_darwin_arm64=z3-5.3.3-arm64-osx-13.3.zip
Z3_ASSET_SIZE_darwin_arm64=53744860
Z3_ASSET_SHA256_darwin_arm64=6957e6c75266d7ca8fa77030e86e83d78624567dcdf34cc11f4192fdc6f93c6b
Z3_BIN_SHA256_darwin_arm64=9b3df8db3324ac2de9ebdd2841477366ecad0626656f806c2168ebf2732745a4

Z3_ASSET_darwin_x86_64=z3-5.3.3-x64-osx-13.3.zip
